Good news first: the pilot actually worked — loss dropped from 21.43 to 12.15 over 10 epochs, so the pipeline (fixed rotation, fixed BCD generation) is functioning correctly.

But missing last.pt is a real problem, not expected. My train.py code saves last.pt unconditionally after every single epoch (not just at the end) — so if all 10 epochs ran and logged, there's no code path that should have skipped writing it 10 times in a row.

Quick things to check, briefly:

Search the exact path, case-sensitive: runs/pilot/last.pt — confirm --out-dir ./runs/pilot is really where it looked, not a different runs/ folder created elsewhere (e.g. if the script was run from a different working directory than expected).
Check the tail of the console output for a silent torch.save failure — permission error, disk full, or antivirus blocking write to that folder would throw an exception right after the log line printed, which could explain "logs exist but no checkpoint."
Check the folder's file list directly (dir runs\pilot or ls runs/pilot), not just a search tool — some file-search tools skip .pt files or don't refresh cache immediately after a process just exited.

Ask Cursor to run dir /s runs\pilot (or ls -la runs/pilot) directly and paste the raw output — that'll settle it faster than a search.
